From: ryoma-89 <ryoma-89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:18:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] gfxstream: optionally send host descriptor pool resets
 without waiting

With VulkanQueueSubmitWithCommands every command carries the process-wide
sequence number and the host applies commands in that order, so a reset
sent now is applied before any later command from any thread. The guest
flushes the reset immediately and leaves the 4-byte status in the
host-to-guest stream; IOStream::readback() consumes such deferred replies
before the next reply (renderControl shares the stream), keeps a non-zero
status, and the next deferred reset returns it. At most 64 replies are
left unread. Opt-in: debug.velox.async_pool_reset=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
